                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">zGround, the datum of the ABL log-law profile: the MODEL-SPACE elevation (m) of the ground the wind enters over — U is 0 at and below it. Leave it unwired and at 0 when the wind case has a Terrain: each wind direction then takes the ground along its own inlet (a Land Cover terrain is RELATIVE to the site, z = 0 at the site centre, so the rim is rarely at 0). Wire it, or type a non-zero value, to hold one value for every direction; without a terrain, the default is 0.</item>
