                    <chunk name="param_input" index="16">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fraction of the domain length in front of the outlet that becomes an absorbing sponge layer relaxing the flow to the inflow profile (OpenLB; 0 = the plain pressure outlet). The pressure outlet bends the profile over the last ~20 % of the domain (measured, 200 m domain: +16 % at 5.5 m, -21 % at 30.5 m at the outlet); a 0.1 sponge keeps the field ahead of it within ~3 %. Treat the sponge zone itself as padding, not as results. At most 0.5.</item>
