                    <chunk name="param_input" index="17">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Turbulent inflow (OpenLB): OpenLB's vortex method adds random eddies to the log-law inlet, sized ~0.4 x the reference height, with the intensity of the log law (I_u = 1/ln(z/z0)), refreshed once per eddy passage. Replaces Jitter. On AIJ Case A it cut the wake's bias from +0.88 to +0.59 and the reattachment length from 2.0 H to 1.3 H against the steady inflow at H/20, and beat the jitter at both resolutions tried (docs/VALIDATION.md 10b), so it is the default, on the CPU and the CUDA solver alike. Off = the steady profile (the validation control). The strip names the arm: synthetic, jitter or steady, as EDDY3D_VALIDATION_INFLOW does.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">8a0c8643-89e4-422c-8888-12ec392d6aab</item>
